## Objective

Replace the foundation Host's synchronous unavailable-provider path with the first live owner-open Codex turn while preserving one active turn lineage per connection and truthful cancellation/error behavior.

## Required source work

- split Host internals into codec, connection, turn state, provider lifecycle, correlation, flow control and error modules;
- add an asynchronous connection loop so control frames remain processable while a provider/tool call runs;
- implement optional `hello`, `turn.start`, `turn.cancel`, `tool.cancel`, window/pause/resume and exactly one `turn.end`;
- allocate stable `connection_id`, `turn_stream_id`, `event_id` and normalized `call_id` values;
- probe the installed runtime using `codex --help` and `codex --version`;
- support an observed full-access invocation form rather than trusting a source asset name;
- parse Codex JSON events, preserve model text and normalize native tool events before publishing them;
- preserve provider stderr/auth/outage/configuration observations without switching provider/model or inventing a semantic HOLD;
- own provider process groups and reap all descendants on cancel/exit.

## State-machine requirements

- one active turn per connection;
- a second turn on the same connection returns `turn_already_active`;
- concurrent turns use separate connections;
- turn cancellation can be processed while provider execution is active;
- duplicate identical turn start attaches/replays; conflicting bytes fail;
- provider-side text without a correlated tool event is never treated as proof of an effect.

## Host tests

- hello and new-turn sequence;
- provider success, deliberate tool failure, continued reasoning and final model text;
- unsupported CLI flag and missing credentials;
- provider crash, cancellation and descendant cleanup;
- slow reader/backpressure and pause/resume without re-execution;
- duplicate/reconnect correlation;
- binary/large event boundaries;
- exactly one terminal turn event.

## Acceptance

A real installed Codex runtime produces provider lifecycle, model, tool and final events on the same bound owner-open turn stream. This issue reaches `HOST_TESTED`; physical Android integration remains W6/W7.

## Dependencies

- PR #1 codec and Host foundation;
- W5 P0 event-record interface should land in parallel before fault qualification.
